PATCH 258: the projectile SPAWN-record chain (b583/b51f -> ba49 -> ba33 -> ba5d + b1df/registrar) --
DGROUP near-offset-as-host-pointer base-losses + the host-pointer-truncated DI arg (SIGSEGV in b1df).

Exposed once the per-frame object UPDATE walk (patch 243, c0e5) reached a type-E emitter object whose
action method (b583, patch 257) spawns a projectile.  The whole spawn chain threads the object through
the DI register as a DGROUP near offset; patch 257 had turned b583's object into a HOST pointer for its
own field derefs, so passing it as a 16-bit call arg TRUNCATED it (g_mem+0x1c000 low16 folded into the
value: real near offset 0xad74 -> corrupt 0x2eb4), and b1df then deref'd that corrupt near offset as a
host int* -> SIGSEGV at FUN_1000_b1df+0x152.

ASM-verified vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin (DS=SS=DGROUP=0x1c00):
 - b583 (0xb583): asm b5d8/b5de pass DI = the object NEAR OFFSET to bbb7/ba49.  Recover it from the
   host pointer param_2 (= g_mem+0x1c000+di, invariant across the sector loop) instead of truncating.
 - FUN_0000_ba49 (0xba49): di=object near offset in param_3 (asm leaves si=di=object after ba33);
   writes the launch velocity dword[si+4]/[si+8] from DAT_2000_5c7f/5c83.  Ghidra used the host object
   ptr param_2 and 16-bit-truncated the dwords.  Rebuilt in the DGROUP model, full dword reads.
 - FUN_0000_ba33 (0xba33): registers the object via b1df(4,di) then installs the spawn template via
   ba5d.  Threaded b1df's CF (g_fist_cf) that Ghidra dropped, and fixed ba5d's template/object args
   (unaff_CS garbage).
 - FUN_0000_ba5d (0xba5d): template->object field copy (bx=template near, si=di=object near).  Ghidra
   base-lost every DS access (host-ptr deref).  Rebuilt with explicit DGROUP byte/word offsets; the 3
   trailing dword self-copies (di==si) kept verbatim.
 - FUN_1000_b1df (0x1b1df): the display-object registrar.  di=object near offset in param_2; b21d
   (patch 200) already returns the roster slot + g_fist_cf.  Finds a free slot in the 182-entry table
   @ DGROUP:0xdfbc (stride 4), stores the near offset, bumps the refcount, zeroes the object body.
   Ghidra deref'd the near offset as a host int* (*param_2 -> SIGSEGV), walked the table at host-int
   stride 8, and dropped b21d's CF.
 - b51f (0xb51f): its own asm b57f ba49 call passes DI = the restored original object; thread
   (uint16)param_1 instead of the dropped unaff_CS.

NOTE (documented deviation, not fixed here): b51f's asm sets c31e's object = SI = DAT_2000_5a25 (the
bb64-found target), but the committed chain dispatches c31e on the original object (param_1).  Left as
observed to keep b583 reachable/crash-free; revisit with the bb64 DAT_5a25 population.  Mission-cascade
only (the 19 menu/dialog flows never register a spawn object).
